# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
.idea/


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This project
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `build/` is already ignored above: erc.rpt, drc.rpt and verify.net are pure
# check output and say nothing a rerun would not.
#
# `fab/` and `cycfi-nu-hub/` are deliberately NOT ignored. fab/ORDER.md is a
# *source* file -- it is written by hand and verify.py asserts the board's
# figures against it -- so ignoring fab/ would drop the one document the
# generators cannot regenerate. And tracking the built board and the
# fabrication zip is what pins a deliverable to the commit it was ordered
# from.

# Per-user KiCad state: window layout, selected layer, last-used tool. Written
# by pcbnew.SaveBoard() on every build, and part of nobody's design.
cycfi-nu-hub/*.kicad_prl

# KiCad's auto-backup zips, created when the project is opened in the GUI.
cycfi-nu-hub/*-backups/
fp-info-cache

# The unzipped staging copy of the gerbers. build.sh deletes and rebuilds it
# every run, and cycfi-nu-hub-pcbway.zip beside it holds byte-identical
# content -- so tracking both means ~1100 lines of churn per build for a
# second copy of the same thing. The zip is the deliverable; this is scratch.
fab/*-pcbway/

# JetBrains module file. Per-user editor state, not part of the design.
*.iml
